  "content": "But it was Moss's vision of a live lab for hackers to uncover vulnerabilities in electronic voting machines and systems that placed him in the national political limelight. DEF CON opened the doors with its inaugural Voting Machine Village at the 2017 conference at Caesars Palace in Las Vegas, and within minutes, hackers found vulnerabilities in several systems. Voting Village in the ensuring years has attracted high-level federal, state and local government officials, including California Sen. Alex Padilla, then the Secretary of State in California, and former CISA director Chris Krebs, who keynoted the event in 2019 .",
